1.0 | A live playground: type on the left, watch it change on the right.
The every-trick page, listing the entire made-up language in one place.
Colors, text effects, headings, lists, tables, callouts, code blocks and emoji.
Copy any example, or open it straight in the playground.

2.0 | Renamed the whole thing to Markdowntastic, with a brand new logo.
Light and dark mode, with a switch in the header. It starts in light mode.
Fixed motion & magic — the effects actually move now.
New ??? block: turns a question into a big proper title.
11 new tricks in total, including speech bubbles, keycaps, sticky notes and captions.
Dash lists now use dashes instead of dots, so they finally look different.
Removed the Surprise me button. You're the surprise now.

2.5 | 10 new decorations: wings, halos, horns, eyes, crowns, cat ears, a mustache, flames, tentacles and lightning.
Colors now recolor everything, including footnotes and decorated tricks: (red"~a red footnote~").
Stack tricks with a + — (blue+glow"like this") or (wave+wings"like that"). One color, as many effects as you want.
Glowing things take a color too: glow, neon, sparkle, halo and lightning all glow in whatever color you give them.
New Somewhat useful section with (line-middle) and (line-right) for aligning the rest of a line.
Fixed the logo not showing up in light mode.

FUTURE PLANS
3.0 Plan: save as png, save as pdf, save as code and load code to show someone's text (useful for previews with interactible things like spoilers or links)
